# Prequel Slider — a Prequel-style ruler slider (Skia tick paths, snapping spring per tick, haptic per tick) driving a GL "butterfly wave scrawler" shader transition over a remote photo, a donut progress ring and a blue→orange indicator colour.
# What this test covers: slow drags through the transition, dragging to the far end (clamped, progress 1) and past it,
# a fast fling whose snap spring (damping 10) overshoots the ends (progress slightly <0 / >1 into the shader,
# donut and interpolateColor), grabbing the ruler mid-spring (cancelAnimation), tiny one-tick drags, and back to 0.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/prequel-slider"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 3000
# Slow drag into the middle of the transition.
gesture pan 350 765 -250 0 900
wait 1200
# Drag to the far end and past it (clamped).
gesture pan 350 765 -300 0 900
wait 1200
# Fling back toward 0: the snap spring overshoots the start.
gesture pan 100 765 280 0 120
wait 1500
# Fling to the end: overshoots progress 1.
gesture pan 380 765 -360 0 120
wait 1500
# Fling, then grab mid-spring.
gesture pan 90 765 290 0 120
wait 150
press 200 765
wait 1000
# One-tick nudges.
gesture pan 200 765 -12 0 400
wait 600
gesture pan 200 765 -12 0 400
wait 600
gesture pan 200 765 12 0 400
wait 600
# Back to the start slowly and beyond.
gesture pan 90 765 300 0 900
wait 600
gesture pan 90 765 300 0 900
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
